     1	# Ward rostering rules
     2	
     3	These rules decide whether a four-week ward roster can be worked and what its
     4	penalty is. They are the rules `tools/check_roster.py` applies.
     5	
     6	## The ward
     7	
     8	Each file in `wards/` is one ward's roster period. It has `days` days, numbered
     9	from 0; day 0 is a Monday, so days 5 and 6 are the first Saturday and Sunday,
    10	days 12 and 13 the second weekend, and so on. Nothing before day 0 or after
    11	the last day is taken into account.
    12	
    13	There are three shifts: `E` (early), `L` (late) and `N` (night), and
    14	`shift_hours` gives the hours each one counts for. A night belongs to the day
    15	it starts on.
    16	
    17	A nurse has an `id`, a `grade` (`senior`, `RN` or `HCA`; a senior nurse is also
    18	a registered nurse, an `HCA` is not), `min_hours` and `max_hours` for the whole
    19	period, `max_nights` for the whole period, a list of `leave` days, and a list of
    20	`requests`. A request `{"day": d, "off": "day"}` asks not to work on day `d` at
    21	all; `{"day": d, "off": "E"}` (or `"L"`, `"N"`) asks not to work that shift on
    22	day `d`.
    23	
    24	`cover[s]` gives, for shift `s`, the `minimum` number of nurses on duty, how
    25	many of them must be `registered` nurses, and the `preferred` number on duty.
    26	`rules` gives `max_consecutive_days`, `rest_days_after_nights` and
    27	`max_weekends`; `weights` gives the price of each soft rule below.
    28	
    29	## Hard rules
    30	
    31	A roster gives every nurse exactly one code per day: `E`, `L`, `N`, or `.` for
    32	a day off. It must keep all of these:
    33	
    34	1. On every day, every shift has at least its `minimum` nurses on duty, at
    35	   least its `registered` count of senior or RN nurses among them, and at least
    36	   one senior nurse.
    37	2. A nurse on leave on a day has `.` that day.
    38	3. Rest between days: a night is not followed the next day by an early or a
    39	   late, and a late is not followed the next day by an early.
    40	4. A nurse works at most `max_consecutive_days` days in a row (any shift counts
    41	   as a working day).
    42	5. After a run of nights, the nurse rests: when a nurse works `N` on day `d`
    43	   and not `N` on day `d + 1`, days `d + 1` up to `d + rest_days_after_nights`
    44	   (those that exist) are days off. A run of nights may go on for as many days
    45	   as rules 4 and 3 allow.
    46	
    47	## Penalty
    48	
    49	A valid roster's penalty is the sum of:
    50	
    51	- `short_of_preferred` for each nurse missing from a shift's `preferred`
    52	  number on each day (nothing for nurses above it);
    53	- for each nurse, `hour_under` for each hour worked below `min_hours`, and
    54	  `hour_over` for each hour above `max_hours`;
    55	- for each nurse, `night_over` for each night above `max_nights`;
    56	- for each nurse and each weekend (Saturday and the Sunday after it), 
    57	  `split_weekend` when the nurse works exactly one of the two days;
    58	- for each nurse, `weekend_over` for each weekend above `max_weekends` on which
    59	  the nurse works at least one of the two days;
    60	- for each nurse, `lone_day` for each working day with a day off both before
    61	  and after it (the first and last day of the period never count);
    62	- `request` for each request not kept: a day-off request is broken by any shift
    63	  on that day, a shift request only by that shift.
    64	
    65	Penalties are whole numbers, and lower is better.
    66	
    67	## File format
    68	
    69	    {"roster": {"A01": "EELL..NN..E...", "A02": "...", ...}}
    70	
    71	Every nurse of the ward appears once, keyed by id, with a string of exactly
    72	`days` characters, one per day in order, each `E`, `L`, `N` or `.`. Unknown
    73	nurse ids are an error. Any other top-level key is ignored.

